cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Zodiacally Ephemeris in research or publications, please cite it as below."
title: "Zodiacally Ephemeris"
abstract: >-
  A table-driven ephemeris for astrological software in pure JavaScript (Node.js): apparent
  geocentric ecliptic longitudes and speeds of the Sun, Moon, Mercury to Pluto, Chiron and the
  true lunar node for 1899-2101, built from NASA/JPL DE440s and, for Chiron, the JPL Horizons
  orbit solution JPL#171, with IAU 2006 sidereal time and Placidus and whole-sign houses.
  Compared with the Swiss Ephemeris and NASA/JPL Horizons in a reproducible benchmark.
  Source-available and free to use, also commercially, with attribution; not an OSI open-source
  licence (attribution in readings shown to others, no distribution as a standalone library).
  See the licence.
type: software
